Open source build fixes for EdenFS (applied by nix/edenfs/default.nix).

Upstream's CMake/Cargo build of EdenFS (build/fbcode_builder/manifests/eden)
has bit-rotted against the current sources; this patch makes it build and run:

* CMake: sources that became header-only (InodeNumber, PrettyPrinters), the
  eden/fs/store/hg -> sl rename, missing targets (privhelper/priority,
  inodes/fscatalog_dev, sigbus_memops, InodeCatalog split out to break a
  dependency cycle), liburing linkage, cxx bridges for redirect_ffi and
  backtrace_ffi (plus -Wl,--wrap=__cxa_throw for ThrowTraceCapture).
* Rust: all Rust code linked into edenfs is built as one staticlib
  (eden/fs/rust/oss-rust-ffi) to avoid duplicate std/cxx symbols; open
  source stand-ins for Meta-internal crates (edenfs-telemetry, the
  "thriftclients" Thrift flavour) and code paths (iobuf, cpe/remote configs,
  lmdb bench, Manifold upload, fbinit); backingstore needs repo's "wdir".
* Python CLI: generated with thrift-python (as the CLI imports
  `*.thrift_types`) instead of the deprecated "py" generator; zipapp mtimes.
* C++ fixes for GCC 16 / fmt 12 (ambiguous not_null conversion, formatting
  std::atomic and a thrift enum).

